   - **Wrestling & Tag Teams:**
     - *Terry Gene Bollea:* Better known as **Hulk Hogan**. His iconic WWF/WCW tag team alongside "Macho Man" Randy Savage (managed by Miss Elizabeth) was **The Mega Powers**. (He was also in "The Mega-Maniacs" with Brutus Beefcake).

   - **Film Industry & Shared Nationalities:**
     - *Aram Avakian & Wilfred Lucas:* Share **American** nationality. Aram Avakian (1926–1987) was an Armenian-American film director/editor (*Jazz on a Summer's Day*, *End of the Road*). Wilfred Lucas (1871–1940) was a Canadian-born American actor, director, and screenwriter.

   - **Airports & Geography:**
     - *Garden City Regional Airport (GCK):* Located in Finney County, **Kansas**. Serviced under the Essential Air Service program.
     - *Valdez Airport (VDZ / Pioneer Field):* State-owned public airport in the Valdez-Cordova Census Area, **Alaska**.

   - **Anime & Voice Acting:**
     - *Max Mittelman:* Voice actor who voices **Saitama** in the English dub of *One-Punch Man* (a webcomic created by ONE; "Wanpanman" is a play on "Anpanman" and "wanpanchi"). Saitama, bored by the absence of challenge in fighting evil, seeks to find **a worthy opponent**. Other roles of Mittelman include Kousei Arima (*Your Lie in April*), King (*The Seven Deadly Sins*), Ritsu Kageyama (*Mob Psycho 100*), Inaho Kaizuka (*Aldnoah.Zero*), and Ryuji Sakamoto (*Persona 5*).

   - **Literature & Millennium Series:**
     - *Mikael Blomkvist:* Created by Stieg Larsson (and later written by David Lagercrantz in *The Girl in the Spider's Web*). His primary profession is **investigative journalist**. Avoid padding the answer with extra titles like "publisher".

